senses.gloss:
Prātar as a denotation of time signifies the ‘early morning’
in the Rigveda^1 and later.^2 Cf. Ahan.
1) i. 125, 1; ii. 18, 1; iii. 41, 2; 52, 1;
iv. 35, 7; v. 76, 3, etc.
2) Av. iv. 11, 12; vi. 128, 2; vii. 101, 1;
xi. 2, 16; Kāṭhaka Saṃhitā, xxxii. 7;
Aitareya Brāhmaṇa, ii. 31; iii. 22. 44;
iv. 20; Śatapatha Brāhmaṇa, xi. 5, 1,
12; Chāndogya Upaniṣad, v. 11, 7,
etc.
